Subject: [PATCH] irqchip/gic-v3-its: Zero allocations after sharing pages

A confidential-computing state transition need not preserve the contents
of an allocation. Restore the __GFP_ZERO contract after successfully
sharing the pages with set_memory_decrypted().

---
 drivers/irqchip/irq-gic-v3-its.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/irqchip/irq-gic-v3-its.c b/drivers/irqchip/irq-gic-v3-its.c
index e9807af23537..48868bf7349c 100644
--- a/drivers/irqchip/irq-gic-v3-its.c
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/irq-gic-v3-its.c
@@ -231,6 +231,13 @@ static struct page *its_alloc_pages_node(int node, gfp_t gfp,
 	if (ret)
 		return NULL;
 
+	/*
+	 * A confidential-computing state transition need not preserve the old
+	 * contents. Restore the allocation contract after the page is shared.
+	 */
+	if (gfp & __GFP_ZERO)
+		memset(page_address(page), 0, PAGE_SIZE << order);
+
 	return page;
 }
 
